  {
   "id": 535889,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/c26077e719fb9702.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Cmglee/Wikipedia, CC BY-SA 3.0)\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The table shows the hearing range of some animals.</p>\n<p>What is a conclusion we can draw from this data?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1049835,
     "content_html": "Elephants can hear higher pitched sounds than humans can."
    },
    {
     "id": 1049836,
     "content_html": "A gerbil would not be able hear a sound at 40 kHz."
    },
    {
     "id": 1049837,
     "content_html": "Dolphins and whales can hear extremely high pitched sounds compared to humans."
    },
    {
     "id": 1049838,
     "content_html": "A sheep cannot hear a sound that is louder than 1 kHz."
    }
   ],
